{
  "description": "stocky bearded Three Kingdoms infantryman seen strictly from the front, black and red armor, red headband, one dark spear with one silver wavy blade and one gold butt cap",
  "action": "Forceful grounded short spear thrust to the exact center of the opponent, not an overhead strike or sideways slash. Load weight, drive with the leading knee, snap the shoulders and hands towards the target center, stop on contact, retract on the identical line, return upright. Keep one rigid wavy spear blade and gold butt; both hands stay on shaft during effort. Keep the rear hand at belt level snug to the right hip, with right elbow close to the body and the left hand leading along the shaft. Hands never swap; no twisted wrist or crossed elbows. Rotate only the thrust axis to the center; the far side of the shaft is occluded by rear armor where it projects over it. Preserve armor and fixed knot with a slight delayed headband tail.",
